msgid "Connection Info for Support Engineers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:5
#: bced11af9a3940d78974cc09dd3ec581
msgid "Partner Support Proxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:7
#: d9216abbcc6642ae862aabf30d246374
msgid "This page tells you how to take advantage of the ArduPilot MAVLink support proxy at `support.ardupilot.org <https://support.ardupilot.org>`__. You have likely been directed here by an ArduPilot support engineer who is wanting you to use the proxy to allow the support engineer to connect to your vehicle to assist you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:14
#: 6dabf70e1d4048dabd1bdff102e6b9ae
msgid "About the Support Proxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:16
#: 681f106988fb4f1883216ab1f7ff2b33
msgid "The ArduPilot partner support proxy allows users vehicles running ArduPilot to connect to a support engineer. Key features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:19
#: 801ef6e4c33344868a777c4afa5eb295
msgid "uses MAVLink2 signing to maintain security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:20
#: aaa664ec9755494c98089ba1d7ffefe6
msgid "does not need a public IP address for either user or support engineer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:23
#: 89e5e318b70040089e3aac0c8f530861
msgid "Connecting to the Support Proxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:25
#: 18ede5bfd9bf4a168c00b6038fff7428
msgid "Your support engineer will have given you a number which you should use when connecting. It will be a 5 or 6 digit number. In the diagrams below we will use the example number '10001'. Please replace that with the number you have been told to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:30
#: 120b619de5f34a29a8e7c022591fec20
msgid "To get started, select the Support Proxy option under Setup->Advanced in MissionPlanner:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:36
#: d81c66762c344370aca30811ff8cbf9e
msgid "If you don't see this option then you have an old version of MissionPlanner and should update to the latest release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:39
#: 8ca2b202d56649abb25ef51d461c2143
msgid "Next enter the 5 or 6 digit ID that your support engineer have you and press connect:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:44
#: f6bf180409884e07a36495eb64449c12
msgid "at this point you are streaming your mavlink data to the proxy server. The support person will be able to connect and help you. You can click the Stop button to stop forwarding your link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:50
#: f62471cc92db4a81bf21bc4c7003da57
msgid "Please close MissionPlanner completely when you have finished with your support session to ensure the port is released."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:54
#: a5326d6c8e1548848ad362d9fa0cc1be
msgid "Connecting with QGroundControl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:56
#: 4972ee218d834020a210f2d1fdcaf01c
msgid "To forward your connection to the support engineer from QGroundControl you need to use this configuration setting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:62
#: 8c2edb04c2d14b809067a88c04ce30ff
msgid "You need to put support.ardupilot.org:XXXXX where XXXXX is the support port number your support engineer has given you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:67
#: a6f0d3800d9a490eae86b18cb26cb485
msgid "Please remember to untick the \"Enable MAVLink forwarding\" option when your support session is completed!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:75
#: 3caef08c6b104d9fa8878581bbfc4a29
msgid "Connecting With MavProxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:77
#: 51fba1f44dc144f9a73bb0b282fb1b2f
msgid "If you use mavproxy instead of MissionPlanner then you should add connect like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:83
#: ce11f79fc09042e8b2bdbacf4119bf1b
msgid "or instead you can do “output add support.ardupilot.org:10001” from an already connected session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:86
#: c05b64b3f2634086bfe0f4a59f22e74d
msgid "CAN Management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:88
#: d355bc984d344a77ba96c702be7de9a5
msgid "Note that as CAN packets can be forwarded over MAVLink you can configure DroneCAN devices remotely via the proxy. Use the MAVLink-CAN1 or MAVLink-CAN2 buttons in Setup->Optional Hardware->DroneCAN to start looking at the remote CAN bus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:94
#: 1f938fabdc99438bac892977ee248e8f
msgid "The Support Proxy Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy.rst:96
#: 8cce02ac2de24eac80771092292f9aaf
msgid "The proxy has a web dashboard at `support.ardupilot.org/dashboard <https://support.ardupilot.org/dashboard>`__. As an ArduPilot *user* you do not normally need it. It is used by support engineers (and the partner organisation that gave you your connection number) to manage the connection: changing the MAVLink2 signing pass phrase, seeing who is currently connected, and optionally recording the telemetry of a support session for later analysis. If you have been given the pass phrase for your connection you can log in there with your connection number and pass phrase."
msgstr ""

